      "main_statement": "**Theorem 1.** Let $a,b,c$ be positive integers and let $n=a+b+c$. There exists a strictly 3-bicolored Steiner triple system with class sizes $a,b,c$ if and only if\n$$n\\equiv1,3\\pmod6,\\qquad a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-ac-bc=n,$$\nand no two of $a,b,c$ are both equal to 2. We call such a profile admissible."
    },
